WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.029
The answer to check four:
the application owner,

2
00:00:03.029 --> 00:00:06.238
after the false-positive
review, in a change window.

3
00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:07.262
Scene five.

4
00:00:07.262 --> 00:00:11.976
A web application firewall only helps if
nothing can reach the origin around it.

5
00:00:11.976 --> 00:00:16.702
Microsoft Learn says to use the Front Door
service tag and the Front Door ID header

6
00:00:16.702 --> 00:00:21.150
together, because the tag's addresses
are shared by every Front Door customer.

7
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:25.650
The portal's east web app does
both, with this profile's own ID.

8
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.262
The west web app allows the tag alone.

9
00:00:28.262 --> 00:00:30.762
So any customer's Front Door can reach it.

10
00:00:30.762 --> 00:00:33.833
The kit reads each origin's
access restrictions

11
00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.674
and compares the header
with the profile's ID.

12
00:00:36.674 --> 00:00:39.428
And it knows configuration isn't proof:

13
00:00:39.428 --> 00:00:42.580
the guide's test is a
direct request, refused.
